data a_slot_family_charged_a_cpu_share_it_is_not_capped_to: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_slot_family_charged_a_cpu_share_it_is_not_capped_to" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: gunbc.ci.ci_runner_placement host_cpu_allocation divides a host's runner threads by the committed width, which counts the fabric execution slots (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_allocation fabric_execution_slot_identities -- the roster's members, srv1's two since the operator ruling of 2026-11-09, gunbc.design_ruling::srv3_srv4_fabric_slots_serve_ci, returned the four srv3/srv4 slots to GitHub Actions), while those slots' slices render gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired gunbc_runner_slot_cpu_quota = SlotCpuQuotaUnbounded. The fold reserves a share for a family that is not held to it, so the host's CPU is not conserved: a busy fabric cell can take the threads the runner slots' quotas were sized against.",

    "HARM: runner slots throttled at their quota while an uncapped fabric cell exceeds its reserved share. WHEN THIS ROW WAS WRITTEN the roster held four slots on srv3/srv4 whose runners were not commissioned, so the harm was future; since 2026-11-09 the roster's members sit on srv1, which is also a serving GitHub runner host (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.network_receipt_decoded_against_workload_population records ten enrolled srv1 runner TAPs at 83dcbb4d6ab, 2026-10-09), so the fold's phantom share now sits on a host that carries runners rather than on two uncommissioned ones. Whether the contention has materialized is a host read this row does not hold, and it is not claimed.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: two CPU authorities for slots of one host -- the per-host fold for GitHub runner slots and the fleet-wide RunnerSlotDesired row for fabric/microvm/workspace slices -- declared as a deliberate divergence in #14008 and #14053 rather than unified.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (CPUWeight still orders contention). CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- one allocation fold whose per-slot result every slot family's slice renders. NEXT TRIGGER: a fabric execution member sharing a host with live GitHub runner slots -- the roster's shape today, so what is left is the read that establishes the contention; before that lands, gunbc.fabric.fabric_cell_effect fabric_cell_slice_quota_directive must read the per-host fold's per-slot quota instead of gunbc_runner_slot_cpu_quota, or the fold must stop counting fabric members in its divisor.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_runner_placement", decl_name: "host_cpu_allocation"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired", decl_name: "gunbc_runner_slot_cpu_quota"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_cell_effect", decl_name: "fabric_cell_slice_quota_directive"),
  ],
}
